ide the trip. I accepted that POL-NS-24 gives the rider nothing (the driver did arrive and did attempt contact, so no 5.00 SGD goodwill credit is due) and that the suggestion of a pattern of fee-collecting is not evidence about this trip. I did not accept that the trip record independently proves the two messages were sent. I accepted the rider's point that the message leg rests on the impaired chat log. The missing traffic advisory EV-ADVIS-05066-01 (MISSING, weight 0.0) carries no fact and no rule in play needs it. No referral arises: the fee is the policy SGD 5.00, so POL-NS-22's amount check does not fire, and POL-NS-25's repeat-no-show counter is not present on the rider's profile.\n\nOpen question for the reviewer: whether the driver's contact — a call that went unanswered and two messages the rider never opened — genuinely discharged the POL-NS-23 obligation to this rider.",
